id var(--navy)}.cov .event h3{font-size:1.7rem;margin:.25em 0}.cov .lake{background:var(--wash)}.cov .lake-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.1fr;gap:7vw}.cov .lake ul{columns:2;padding-left:20px;line-height:1.8}.cov .lake-map{padding:42px;background:white;border-top:8px solid var(--mustard);box-shadow:0 20px 50px rgba(11,31,58,.1)}.cov .lake-map strong{font-family:Georgia,serif;color:var(--navy);font-size:2rem;font-weight:400}.cov .stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;background:#d8dce0;margin-top:28px}.cov .stat{background:white;padding:25px}.cov .stat b{display:block;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:var(--navy);font-size:2rem}.cov .closing{background:var(--navy);color:white;text-align:center}.cov .closing h2{color:white!important}.cov .closing .logo{position:static;margin:0 auto 36px;width:310px;height:310px;filter:none}.cov .btn{display:inline-block;background:var(--mustard);color:var(--navy)!important;padding:15px 24px;text-decoration:none!important;font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em}.cov .small{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--muted)}\n@media(max-width:850px){.cov .intro,.cov .split,.cov .lake-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cov .cards{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.cov .hero .logo{width:190px;height:190px}.cov .events{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cov .coffee-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}@media(max-width:560px){.cov section{padding:72px 0}.cov .cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cov .hero .logo{display:none}.cov .hero{min-height:650px}.cov .intro-photo,.cov .feature-photo{height:420px}.cov .lake ul{columns:1}.cov .coffee-grid{display:block}.cov .coffee-photo{height:300px;margin-bottom:16px}.cov .closing .logo{width:240px;height:240px}}\n</style>\n<main class=\"cov\">\n<header class=\"hero\"><div class=\"hero-copy\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Rooted In · South King County</div><h1>Living in Covington, Washington</h1><p>Newer neighborhoods, everyday convenience, parks and community events—with Kent, Maple Valley and Black Diamond close enough to borrow whenever the mood strikes.</p></div><img class=\"logo\" src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/19.png\" alt=\"Rooted in Covington logo\"></header>\n<section><div class=\"wrap intro\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">A Covington story</div><h2>Apparently all my friends figured it out before I did.</h2><p>I lived in Covington years ago, and if I’m being completely honest, two of the biggest selling points were having Costco close by and easy access to Trapper’s Sushi. Priorities.</p><p>Back then, Covington still had a little bit of that “way out there” reputation. It felt more country, a little redneck, and definitely wasn’t the place everyone was rushing to move to.</p><p>Fast forward, and somehow <strong>all</strong> of my best friends now live within about a mile of each other in Covington. And yes, I’m a little jealous.</p><p>The city has grown up right along with the people who moved here. There are more restaurants, shopping, neighborhoods and amenities, but it still has that slightly removed-from-the-city feel that made it appealing in the first place. Covington is booming, and apparently all my friends figured it out before I did.</p><p class=\"lede\">So, what’s all the Covington hype about? Let’s dive in.</p></div><div><div class=\"intro-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Mount_Rainier_as_seen_from_a_Covington_neighborhood.jpg\" alt=\"Mount Rainier beyond a Covington neighborhood\"></div><p class=\"photo-credit\">Rainier photograph: <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=90799473\">Yordanpopovbg — Own work, CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"history\"><div class=\"wrap split\"><div class=\"history-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/kent-area-ca-1920-copy.jpg\" alt=\"Historic South King County mill workers and machinery\"></div><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">The roots</div><h2>Prairie, rail lines and a city of its own.</h2><p>The land around present-day Covington was home to the Stkamish, Smulkamis and Skopamish peoples, whose communities were connected to this region’s waterways and prairies. Later known as Jenkins Prairie, the area became a Northern Pacific Railway stop around the turn of the twentieth century.</p><p>Lumber mills rose near Jenkins and Soos creeks; dairies and berry farms carried the community into its next chapter. Covington grew for decades without city limits of its own before residents chose incorporation, officially forming the city in 1997.</p><p class=\"lede\">Its roots are rural, practical and community-minded—qualities that still show up in the pace of life here.</p><a href=\"https://www.historylink.org/File/10337\">Read Covington’s history →</a></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"ticker\"><div class=\"ticker-track\"><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>21,496</b><span>Population</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>7,377</b><span>Households</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>$134,502</b><span>Median household income</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>78.9%</b><span>Homeownership rate</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>$637,300</b><span>Median home value</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>$2,232/mo</b><span>Median rent</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>2.87</b><span>Average household size</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>23.6%</b><span>Under age 18</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>5.93</b><span>Square miles</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>3,503</b><span>People per sq. mile</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>33.4 min.</b><span>Average commute</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>+3.5%</b><span>Growth since 2020</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>21,496</b><span>Population</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>7,377</b><span>Households</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>$134,502</b><span>Median household income</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>78.9%</b><span>Homeownership rate</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>$637,300</b><span>Median home value</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>$2,232/mo</b><span>Median rent</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>2.87</b><span>Average household size</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>23.6%</b><span>Under age 18</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>5.93</b><span>Square miles</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>3,503</b><span>People per sq. mile</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>33.4 min.</b><span>Average commute</span></div><div class=\"ticker-item\"><b>+3.5%</b><span>Growth since 2020</span></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"rule\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Coffee · before work, after work &amp; on the go</div><h2>Coffee, bagels and absolutely no judgment.</h2><div class=\"coffee-grid\"><article class=\"coffee-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cafe-elite.jpeg\" alt=\"A sweet drink from Café Elite\"><div class=\"caption\"><h3>Café Elite</h3><p>Is it coffee or dessert? Either way, sign me up.</p><a style=\"color:white\" href=\"https://cafeelite.com/\">Visit Café Elite →</a></div></article><article class=\"coffee-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Mount_Rainier_as_seen_from_a_Covington_neighborhood.jpg\" alt=\"Covington morning with Mount Rainier nearby\"><div class=\"caption\"><h3>Foss\' Grocery &amp; Espresso</h3><p>Who hasn’t stopped by Foss for a beverage? It gives those small-town vibes you just want to support.</p><a style=\"color:white\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Foss%27+Grocery+%26+Espresso+Covington+WA\">Map it →</a></div></article><article class=\"coffee-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Costco_Covington_big.jpg\" alt=\"Everyday Covington convenience\"><div class=\"caption\"><h3>Bruchelle\'s Bagel Bistro</h3><p>That bagel menu? Drool-worthy. Yum.</p><a style=\"color:white\" href=\"https://bruchelles.com/\">Visit Bruchelle\'s →</a></div></article></div><div class=\"coffee-note\"><strong>Covington definitely understands the quick-coffee lifestyle.</strong> It may not have an abundance of coffeehouses where everyone spends three hours working on a screenplay, but the morning commute is very well covered.</div></div></section>\n<section class=\"feature\"><div class=\"wrap split\"><div class=\"feature-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Nikkis-Resturant.png\" alt=\"Nikki\'s Restaurant and Lounge in Covington\"></div><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">The local diner</div><h2>Nikki\'s Restaurant &amp; Lounge</h2><p class=\"quote\">This is where you go when drive-through coffee isn\'t enough and you actually want eggs, hash browns, pancakes and a server who keeps the coffee coming.</p><p>Nikki\'s is the classic Covington sit-down breakfast spot and a longtime local gathering place.</p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://nikkisrestaurant.com/\">Visit Nikki\'s</a></div></div></section>\n<section><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Local food favorites</div><h2>Worth putting in the rotation.</h2><div class=\"cards\"><article class=\"card\"><h3>Pupusas Locas</h3><p>Salvadoran food, pupusas and plenty of dishes you won\'t find at every other restaurant in town.</p><a href=\"https://pupusaslocaswa.com/\">Visit Pupusas Locas →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Iron Grill</h3><p>Build-your-own Mongolian-style stir fry. Pile the bowl questionably high and hope your engineering skills hold up on the walk to the grill.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theirongrill/\">Find Iron Grill on Facebook →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Trapper\'s Sushi</h3><p>A familiar South King County sushi favorite with a Covington location.</p><a href=\"https://www.trapperssushi.com/\">Visit Trapper\'s Sushi →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Legendary Doughnuts</h3><p>Because sometimes the answer to “Where should we eat?” is simply a giant doughnut.</p><a href=\"https://www.legendarydoughnuts.com/\">Visit Legendary Doughnuts →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Where\'s the best burger?</h3><p>Covington has plenty of burgers, including familiar chains. But Maple Valley and Black Diamond are basically extensions of our restaurant options, and Covington residents are very comfortable borrowing theirs.</p></article></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"rule\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Drinks · stay local or venture a few minutes out</div><h2>Three different moods.</h2><div class=\"cards\"><article class=\"card\"><h3>Pla-Mor Bar &amp; Grill</h3><p>Just outside Covington on the Maple Valley side: casual, unpretentious and a true longtime neighborhood bar-and-grill.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/search/top?q=pla-mor%20bar%20%26%20grill\">Find Pla-Mor on Facebook →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>House &amp; Hazel</h3><p>A few minutes into Maple Valley, with a modern mercantile, restaurant and bar—and a completely different kind of flair.</p><a href=\"https://houseandhazel.com/\">Visit House &amp; Hazel →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Big Block Brewery</h3><p>Head toward Black Diamond for a brewpub and restaurant that\'s another easy option just beyond town.</p><a href=\"https://www.bigblockbrewery.com/black-diamond\">Visit Big Block Brewery →</a></article></div><p class=\"lede\">One of Covington\'s best features is that when you run out of places to go in Covington, Maple Valley and Black Diamond are right there.</p></div></section>\n<section class=\"feature\"><div class=\"wrap split\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">A real community gathering place</div><h2><a style=\"color:white\" href=\"https://www.covingtonwa.gov/parks/covingtoncommunitypark.php\">Covington Community Park</a></h2><p>This newer park has become one of Covington\'s main gathering places, used for recreation, sports and some of the city\'s biggest summer activities.</p><p>Summer concerts, outdoor movies, KidsFest and other community events are exactly the kind of thing Covington does particularly well: family-friendly activities that don\'t require driving into Seattle.</p></div><div class=\"feature-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/images-1.jpeg\" alt=\"Green space and water near Covington\"></div></div></section>\n<section><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Things to do &amp; annual events</div><h2>Somebody is usually planning something.</h2><p class=\"lede\">Covington may not have 47 places to go on a Saturday night, but the community calendar stays busy.</p><div class=\"events\"><article class=\"event\"><h3><a href=\"https://www.covingtonwa.gov/covingtondays/\">Covington Days</a></h3><p>One of the city\'s biggest annual traditions, with a parade, live entertainment, food, vendors, kids\' activities and community events.</p></article><article class=\"event\"><h3><a href=\"https://www.covingtonwa.gov/events/\">KidsFest</a></h3><p>A free annual event at Covington Community Park focused completely on kids, with activities, entertainment and community organizations.</p></article><article class=\"event\"><h3><a href=\"https://www.covingtonwa.gov/events/\">Summer concerts &amp; outdoor movies</a></h3><p>Outdoor concerts and Movies Under the Stars take over Covington Community Park during summer. Check the city calendar for current dates.</p></article><article class=\"event\"><h3><a href=\"https://www.covingtonchamber.org/\">Covington Makers Market</a></h3><p>Local makers, artists, creators, bakers, crafters and businesses, brought together through the Covington Chamber of Commerce and the City.</p></article></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"lake\"><div class=\"wrap lake-grid\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">What\'s coming to Covington</div><h2>LakePointe Urban Village</h2><p class=\"quote\">If you\'ve driven Highway 18 through Covington and wondered, “Are they ever going to do something with that giant gravel pit?”—the answer is yes. Or at least, that\'s the plan.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.covingtonwa.gov/lakepointe/index.php\"><strong>LakePointe Urban Village</strong></a> is the massive mixed-use development planned at Covington\'s northern gateway. The approximately 214-acre master-plan area is envisioned to include:</p><ul><li>Residential neighborhoods</li><li>Commercial and mixed-use development</li><li>Shopping and restaurants</li><li>Public gathering spaces</li><li>Parks and trails</li><li>A central lake/pond feature</li><li>Office space</li><li>Entertainment uses</li></ul><p>The water feature is envisioned as a major public amenity surrounded by places where people can gather, walk, dine, shop and live.</p></div><aside class=\"lake-map\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Official planning materials</div><strong>Master development plan map &amp; project renderings</strong><p>See the City of Covington\'s official project materials for the detailed plan showing the central water feature, residential and mixed-use areas, gathering spaces, parks, trails and circulation.</p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://www.covingtonwa.gov/lakepointe/index.php\">View the official LakePointe plan</a><p class=\"small\">Conceptual plans and renderings only. Final development may differ; buildings, roads, restaurants, trails and amenities are not completed or guaranteed.</p><div class=\"stats\"><div class=\"stat\"><b>~1,750</b>residential units referenced in planning documents</div><div class=\"stat\"><b>~1.3M sq. ft.</b>commercial/retail development referenced in planning documents</div></div><p>Plans have historically included entertainment uses and a movie theater concept—but there is no announced theater operator or confirmed opening date. So don\'t start standing in line for movie tickets just yet.</p></aside></div><div class=\"wrap\"><p class=\"lede\">But if LakePointe ultimately comes together anywhere close to the vision, it could completely change the dining, shopping and entertainment side of Covington.</p></div></section>\n<section><div class=\"wrap split\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">Shopping &amp; everyday convenience</div><h2>Life is close to home.</h2><p>One of Covington\'s biggest practical advantages is that you don\'t have to go far for everyday life. Major grocery stores, restaurants, services, medical care and plenty of everyday shopping are right in town.</p><p class=\"quote\">Maybe Costco isn\'t technically a community amenity, but tell that to anyone who lives five minutes from one.</p></div><div class=\"intro-photo\"><img src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Costco_Covington_big.jpg\" alt=\"Costco in Covington, Washington\"></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"rule\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Living in Covington</div><h2>Why buyers put it on the list.</h2><div class=\"split\"><div><p>Covington tends to have newer housing than many established parts of Renton and Kent, with subdivisions, cul-de-sacs, townhomes and homes built primarily during the last several decades.</p><p>It appeals to people looking for suburban neighborhoods, parks, shopping and convenient access to Highway 18 while remaining close to Maple Valley, Kent and Black Diamond.</p></div><div><p class=\"lede\">The useful question isn\'t whether Covington is “affordable.” It\'s what your budget buys here compared with Renton, Kent, Maple Valley and the rest of South King County.</p><p>That comparison—and how the location fits your actual weekly routine—is where local guidance becomes useful.</p></div></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"closing\"><div class=\"wrap\"><img class=\"logo\" src=\"https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/19.png\" alt=\"Rooted in Covington logo\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Thinking about Covington?</div><h2>Suburban convenience, growing families, and everything you need close to home.</h2><p>Whether you\'re moving in, moving across town or comparing South King County communities, Tanya can help you sort through the options without the pressure.</p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/contact/\">Ask Tanya about Covington</a></div></section>\n</main>\n\n<!-- wp:template-part {\"slug\":\"footer\",\"theme\":\"tanya-barrans\",\"tagName\":\"footer\"} /-->', 'Page: Covington', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '90239-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-08-26 19:13:12', '2026-08-26 19:13:12', '', 90239, 'https://violet-wren-104886.hostingersite.com/?p=90403', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
